  <section class="section" id="architecture">
    <div class="wrap section-head rvl">
      <h2 class="display">Architecture</h2>
      <p class="lede">Seven layers from physical supply to the terminal, and the four tokens that move through them.</p>
      <p class="eyebrow" style="text-align:right;align-self:end">Layers · Tokens</p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap arch rvl">
      <div class="arch-col">
        <div class="arch-h"><span>DEX layers</span><span>top → bottom</span></div>
        <div class="stack">
          <div class="lyr access"><span class="n">07</span><div><b>Application layer</b><small>Terminal · mobile · SDK · institutional API</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr access"><span class="n">06</span><div><b>Off-chain services</b><small>Matching engine · sequencer · market data · keepers</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr fin"><span class="n">05</span><div><b>Exchange programs · Solana</b><small>USDC vault · cross-margin · risk engine · fill settlement</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr fin"><span class="n">04</span><div><b>Settlement layer</b><small>Expiry · final index · cash or physical · insurance fund</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr phys"><span class="n">03</span><div><b>Capacity tokens</b><small>SPL mint per instrument × quarter · operator bond</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr phys"><span class="n">02</span><div><b>Verification &amp; oracles</b><small>Attestation · telemetry · reference index feed</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr phys"><span class="n">01</span><div><b>Physical supply</b><small>Data centres · Openmesh nodes · delivered workloads</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr cross"><span class="n">∥</span><div><b>Cross-cutting</b><small>Governance · security · compliance · instrument design</small></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="legend"><span><i class="phys"></i>Physical stack</span><span><i class="fin"></i>Financial stack</span><span><i class="access"></i>Access</span><span><i class="cross"></i>Cross-cutting</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-col">
        <div class="arch-h"><span>Token layers</span><span>what moves through it</span></div>
        <div class="stack">
          <div class="lyr cross tok"><span class="n">◎</span><div><b>Native token · protocol</b><small>Governance · staking · operator &amp; keeper bonds · fee discounts · insurance backstop · buyback from fees</small></div></div>
          <div class="tok-row">
            <div class="lyr fin tok"><span class="n">LP</span><div><b>LP tokens</b><small>Vault shares · earn maker fees · first-loss backstop</small></div></div>
            <div class="lyr fin tok"><span class="n">POS</span><div><b>Position accounts</b><small>Futures &amp; perps · cross-margin · PnL in USDC</small></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="lyr access tok"><span class="n">$</span><div><b>USDC · settlement</b><small>Collateral · margin · cash settlement · fees</small></div></div>
          <div class="lyr phys tok"><span class="n">CAP</span><div><b>Capacity tokens · physical</b><small>One mint per instrument and delivery quarter · minted on verification, burned on delivery</small></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flows">
          <div><i></i>Native token staked as operator bond → unlocks capacity minting</div>
          <div><i></i>Positions settle to USDC; physical settlement takes delivery of capacity tokens</div>
          <div><i></i>Operators sell capacity tokens forward for USDC before the window opens</div>
          <div><i></i>Trading fees in USDC → treasury → buyback and insurance fund</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

